      "errorMessage": "<task id=\"ses_f499ea33effe3SUdGXRKc1OFg8\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI have everything needed. Here is the complete research report.\n\n---\n\n# Native Inbox page — codebase precedent report (read-only)\n\nAll paths absolute. Nothing was modified.\n\n---\n\n## 0. Key finding up front\n\nChat (P5.2) is the precedent, but **there is no front-end \"nav registry\" to edit**. Navigation entries are DB rows (`NavigationMenuItem`) declared by apps or created by users; the a2e-chat \"Discussions\" nav entry points at a *view*, not at the native `/discussions` route. The native route is currently reached only through the Cmd+K search provider. The server side of your Inbox (topic, publisher, event contract, ACL) **already exists** from P8.1 — but there is **no GraphQL resolver** for notifications yet. Details in §2 and §6.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Routing\n\n### 1a. `AppPath` enum member\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/types/AppPath.ts`\n\n```\n21:   // Onboarded\n22:   AiChat = '/chat/:threadId?',\n23:   // Native workspace chat (a2e-chat objects). Distinct from AiChat's `/chat`.\n24:   Discussions = '/discussions',\n25:   Index = '/',\n26:   // Mobile only: the navigation menu is a page there rather than a drawer.\n27:   Home = '/home',\n28:   TasksPage = '/objects/tasks',\n29:   OpportunitiesPage = '/objects/opportunities',\n```\n\n`AppPath` lives in **`twenty-shared`**, not twenty-front. Per `AGENTS.md` gotchas, after editing it run `npx nx build twenty-shared --skip-nx-cache` before trusting any typecheck in `twenty-front`.\n\n### 1b. Route registration\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/app/routing/utils/createWorkspaceRouteObjects.tsx`\n\nLazy import (lines 44-48):\n```tsx\nconst ChatPage = lazy(() =>\n  import('~/pages/chat/ChatPage').then((module) => ({\n    default: module.ChatPage,\n  })),\n);\n```\n\nRoute object (lines 136-143):\n```tsx\n{\n  path: AppPath.Discussions,\n  element: (\n    <LazyRoute>\n      <ChatPage />\n    </LazyRoute>\n  ),\n},\n```\n\nThe chat route carries **no `handle`**, so it is main-surface-only. Pages that should also open in the side panel declare (see lines 88-91 / 106-109):\n```tsx\nhandle: {\n  workspaceSurfaces: MAIN_AND_SIDE_PANEL,\n  isLocationExpandableFromSidePanel: true,\n},\n```\n\n### 1c. Reading a query param (`channelId`)\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/pages/chat/ChatPage.tsx`\n\n```\n45:   const [searchParams] = useSearchParams();\n...\n61:   // \"Go to channel\" deep link: the Cmd+K provider appends `channelId`, so the\n62:   // page lands on the named channel instead of just the discussions list.\n63:   const requestedChannelId = searchParams.get('channelId');\n...\n67:   useEffect(() => {\n68:     if (\n69:       isDefined(requestedChannelId) &&\n70:       channels.some((channel) => channel.id === requestedChannelId) &&\n71:       requestedChannelId !== selectedChatChannelId\n72:     ) {\n73:       setSelectedChatChannelId(requestedChannelId);\n74:       return;\n75:     }\n...\n87:   }, [channels, requestedChannelId, sections, selectedChatChannelId, setSelectedChatChannelId]);\n```\n\nThe deep link is built with `getAppPath` in\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/chat/utils/mapChatSearchRecordsToResultItems.ts:16-17`:\n```ts\nexport const buildChatChannelSearchPath = (channelId: string): string =>\n  getAppPath(AppPath.Discussions, undefined, { channelId });\n```\ni.e. `/discussions?channelId=<id>`. `getAppPath(path, params, queryParams)` is from `twenty-shared/utils`.\n\n### 1d. Exact additions for an Inbox route\n1. `twenty-shared/src/types/AppPath.ts` — add an onboarded-path member, e.g. `Inbox = '/inbox',` (additive, no collision).\n2. `createWorkspaceRouteObjects.tsx` — add the lazy import:\n```tsx\nconst InboxPage = lazy(() =>\n  import('~/pages/inbox/InboxPage').then((module) => ({\n    default: module.InboxPage,\n  })),\n);\n```\nand the route object:\n```tsx\n{\n  path: AppPath.Inbox,\n  element: (\n    <LazyRoute>\n      <InboxPage />\n    </LazyRoute>\n  ),\n},\n```\n3. If you want a deep link like `/inbox?notificationId=<id>`, mirror §1c exactly.\n4. Rebuild `twenty-shared`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Navigation conventions (P1.2)\n\nThe nav drawer is composed in:\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/navigation/components/MainNavigationDrawerContent.tsx`\n- `.../navigation/components/MainNavigationDrawerNavigationContent.tsx`\n- `.../navigation/components/MainNavigationDrawerScrollableItems.tsx`\n- `.../navigation/components/NavigationDrawerTabbedContent.tsx`\n\n`MainNavigationDrawerScrollableItems.tsx:31-41` renders DB-backed sections:\n```tsx\n<StyledScrollableItemsContainer>\n  <NavigationDrawerOpenedSection />\n  <Suspense fallback={<NavigationDrawerWorkspaceSectionSkeletonLoader />}>\n    <FavoritesSectionDispatcher />\n    <WorkspaceSectionDispatcher />\n  </Suspense>\n</StyledScrollableItemsContainer>\n```\n\n**There is no hard-coded front array of nav items.** The P1.2 phase report states this explicitly:\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/docs/plan/phases/phase-01-report.md:118-119`\n> \"Nav visibility: verified no extension needed — nav items are DB rows owned by the app; uninstall deletes them with the metadata sync; no code change.\"\n\nNav item types `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/types/NavigationMenuItemType.ts`:\n```ts\nexport enum NavigationMenuItemType {\n  VIEW = 'VIEW',\n  FOLDER = 'FOLDER',\n  LINK = 'LINK',\n  OBJECT = 'OBJECT',\n  RECORD = 'RECORD',\n  PAGE_LAYOUT = 'PAGE_LAYOUT',\n}\n```\n`LINK` is **external-only** — `.../navigation-menu-item/display/link/utils/getLinkNavigationMenuItemComputedLink.ts:6-10` prepends `https://` to anything not already `http(s)`. It cannot point at `/inbox`. `OBJECT`/`VIEW`/`RECORD`/`PAGE_LAYOUT` resolve to record-object routes (`getNavigationMenuItemComputedLink.ts:23-50`).\n\n### Where the chat/discussions nav entry is\nIt is an **app-declared nav item**, not front code:\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-chat/src/navigation-menu-items/channels.navigation-menu-item.ts`\n```ts\nexport default defineNavigationMenuItem({\n  universalIdentifier: NAVIGATION_MENU_ITEM_IDS.channels,\n  name: 'Discussions',\n  icon: 'IconMessages',\n  position: 130,\n  type: NavigationMenuItemType.VIEW,\n  viewUniversalIdentifier: VIEW_IDS.allChannels,\n});\n```\nIt opens the `chatChannel` record index — **not** the native `/discussions` page.\n\n### Reachability gap (documented, not a bug)\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/docs/plan/phases/phase-05-report.md:71`\n> \"the route is registered but nothing links to it yet — the a2e-chat app's `Discussions` nav item is `VIEW → chatChannels` … pointing the app nav/command at `AppPath.Discussions` (or a `LINK` nav row) is the next wiring step\"\n\n`:74`\n> \"`P5.2-chat-live` — … add Cmd+K 'go to channel' (which can also wire the nav to `/discussions`).\"\n\n### How native chat is actually reached today\nVia Cmd+K: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/chat/hooks/useChatSearchResultItems.ts` (provider) → merged in `.../side-panel/pages/search/components/SidePanelSearchRecordsPage.tsx:3,48,78`. Provider items carry a `path` built from `AppPath`.\n\n**Implication for Inbox:** there is no `NavigationDrawer` array to add an Inbox entry to. To make `/inbox` reachable, follow the chat precedent (Cmd+K provider / deep-link) or add a new DB `NavigationMenuItem` mechanism. A native top-level route cannot be surfaced by the existing `LINK` nav type because it is HTTPS-only.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Chat page + feature module structure\n\n### 3a. Feature module files\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/chat/`\n\n- `components/` — `ChatSidebar.tsx`, `ChatChannelConversation.tsx`, `ChatMessageList.tsx`, `ChatMessageBody.tsx`, `ChatThreadView.tsx`, `ChatComposer.tsx`, plus `__tests__/`.\n- `hooks/` — `useChatChannels.ts`, `useChatChannel.ts`, `useChatMessages.ts`, `useChatUnreadCounts.ts`, `useChatChannelLive.ts`, `useSendChatMessage.ts`, `useSendChatMessageWithQueue.ts`, `useSendChatTypingIndicator.ts`, `useMarkChatChannelRead.ts`, `useChatMentionCandidates.ts`, `useChatWorkspaceMembers.ts`, `useChatAuthorLabels.ts`, `useChatSearchResultItems.ts`, `useOpenChatChannelInSidePanel.ts`, `useRecordChatChannels.ts`, plus `__tests__/`.\n- `graphql/queries/` — `chatMessagesQuery.ts`, `chatUnreadCountsQuery.ts`; `graphql/mutations/sendChatTypingIndicatorMutation.ts`.\n- `states/` — `selectedChatChannelIdState.ts`, `chatComposerDraftState.ts`, `expandedChatThreadParentIdState.ts`, `focusedChatThreadParentIdState.ts`.\n- `types/` — `ChatChannel.ts`, `ChatMessage.ts`, `ChatRealtimeEvent.ts`.\n- `utils/` — `buildChatChannelTopic.ts`, `applyChatRealtimeEventToMessages.ts`, `groupChatChannelsBySection.ts`, `getChatReadState.ts`, `splitChatMessageBody.ts`, `chatMentionDraft.ts`, `chatOfflineQueue.ts`, `mapChatSearchRecordsToResultItems.ts`, `buildChatThreadReplyMap.ts`, `recordChatChannel.ts`, plus `__tests__/`.\n- `constants/` — `ChatChannelSectionOrder.ts`, `ChatEmojiPalette.ts`.\n- `side-panel/` — `states/viewableChatChannelIdComponentState.ts`, `components/SidePanelChatChannelPage.tsx`.\n\nPage: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/pages/chat/ChatPage.tsx` (119 lines).\n\n### 3b. Page composition\n`ChatPage.tsx:43-118` — local Jotai selection state + hooks, then:\n```tsx\n<StyledChatPage data-testid=\"chat-page\">\n  <ChatSidebar sections={sections} selectedChannelId={...} unreadCountByChannelId={...} onSelectChannel={...} />\n  <StyledConversation>\n    <RealtimeReconnectBanner />\n    {isDefined(selectedChannel) ? (\n      <ChatChannelConversation channel={selectedChannel} />\n    ) : (\n      <StyledEmptyConversation>{t`Select a channel to start chatting`}</StyledEmptyConversation>\n    )}\n  </StyledConversation>\n</StyledChatPage>\n```\nThe conversation surface is extracted (`ChatChannelConversation.tsx`) so page and side-panel mini-chat share it. `ChatPage.tsx:8-16` shows imports: own feature via `@/chat/...`, cross-cutting realtime via `~/modules/realtime/...`.\n\n### 3c. Data fetching patterns\nTwo patterns coexist:\n\n**App-owned metadata objects → shared object-record machinery**\n`useChatChannels.ts`:\n```ts\nconst { records, loading, error } = useFindManyRecords({\n  objectNameSingular: 'chatChannel',\n  recordGqlFields: { id: true, name: true, kind: true, visibility: true, topic: true },\n  limit: 200,\n});\n```\n`useChatChannel.ts` uses `useFindOneRecord` with `skip`. Signature of `useFindManyRecords` is over at `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/hooks/useFindManyRecords.ts:26-48` (`{ objectNameSingular, filter?, orderBy?, skip?, recordGqlFields?, limit? }`).\n\n**Server custom resolvers → hand-written Apollo query with `useApolloCoreClient`**\n`useChatUnreadCounts.ts`:\n```ts\nconst apolloCoreClient = useApolloCoreClient();\nconst { data, loading, error } = useQuery<ChatUnreadCountsQueryResult>(\n  CHAT_UNREAD_COUNTS_QUERY,\n  { client: apolloCoreClient },\n);\n```\nThe `gql` document lives in `modules/chat/graphql/queries/chatUnreadCountsQuery.ts:7-18`, exporting the document plus a result type. `useChatMessages.ts` is the same pattern with variables + `skip: channelId === null`.\n\nInbox will need this second pattern: **a `notifications` GraphQL query does not exist yet** (§6).\n\n### 3d. Empty / loading states\n- Empty conversation: `ChatPage.tsx:34-41` (`StyledEmptyConversation`) + `t\\`Select a channel to start chatting\\``.\n- Empty sidebar list: `ChatSidebar.tsx:133-134` → `<StyledEmptyState>{t\\`No channels yet\\`}</StyledEmptyState>`.\n- Loading: `ChatPage` passes `loading` through but renders no spinner; `ChatSidebar` shows the empty state (no dedicated skeleton in chat — note `RecordIndexSkeletonLoader` exists if you want one).\n- `RealtimeReconnectBanner` (from `~/modules/realtime/components/`) is always rendered above the conversation.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Realtime\n\n### 4a. Hook signature\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/realtime/hooks/useRealtimeTopic.ts:14-25`\n```ts\nexport const useRealtimeTopic = <TPayload>({\n  topic,\n  onEvent,\n  enabled = true,\n}: {\n  topic: string;\n  onEvent?: (payload: TPayload, envelope: RealtimeEnvelope) => void;\n  enabled?: boolean;\n}): {\n  lastEnvelope: RealtimeEnvelope | null;\n  lastError: RealtimeEnvelope | null;\n} => {\n```\nImportant detail (`:61-64`): `onEvent` is intentionally **not** a dependency; consumers pass inline closures. Reconnect catch-up is the consumer's job. Errors (subscription refused/auth) surface via `lastError`, separate from events.\n\n### 4b. Front chat topic builder (your template)\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/chat/utils/buildChatChannelTopic.ts`\n```ts\n// Chat realtime topics follow the gateway grammar `workspace:<id>:chat:<id>`\n// (server parse-realtime-topic.util.ts). The builder mirrors the server\n// `chat-topic.util.ts` so subscribe and publish name the channel identically.\nexport const buildChatChannelTopic = ({ workspaceId, channelId }: {\n  workspaceId: string; channelId: string;\n}): string => `workspace:${workspaceId}:chat:${channelId}`;\n```\n\n### 4c. Example call (subscription)\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/chat/hooks/useChatChannelLive.ts:40-41,90-134`\n```ts\nconst currentWorkspace = useAtomStateValue(currentWorkspaceState);\nconst workspaceId = currentWorkspace?.id ?? null;\n...\nconst topic =\n  isDefined(workspaceId) && isDefined(channelId)\n    ? buildChatChannelTopic({ workspaceId, channelId })\n    : '';\n\nuseRealtimeTopic<ChatRealtimeEvent>({\n  topic,\n  enabled: topic.length > 0,\n  onEvent: (event) => {\n    if (event.type === CHAT_TYPING_EVENT_TYPE) { /* ... */ return; }\n    if (!isChatRealtimeMessageEvent(event)) return;\n    setRealtimeMessageEvents((currentEvents) => [...currentEvents, event]);\n  },\n});\n```\nThe event union is mirrored client-side in `modules/chat/types/ChatRealtimeEvent.ts` because the server domain events are not in the metadata codegen surface (`:4-6`).\n\n### 4d. The server Inbox topic + contract ALREADY EXIST\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/notification/utils/inbox-topic.util.ts`\n```ts\nexport const buildInboxTopic = ({\n  workspaceId, userId,\n}: { workspaceId: string; userId: string }): string =>\n  `workspace:${workspaceId}:inbox:${userId}`;\n```\n\nEvent payload — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/notification/utils/notification-realtime-event.util.ts`:\n```ts\nexport const NOTIFICATION_INBOX_UPDATED_EVENT_TYPE = 'notification.inbox.updated';\n\nexport type NotificationRealtimeEntry = {\n  id: string; type: string;\n  payload: Record<string, unknown> | null;\n  createdAt: string; readAt: string | null; archivedAt: string | null;\n};\n\nexport type NotificationInboxRealtimeEvent = {\n  type: typeof NOTIFICATION_INBOX_UPDATED_EVENT_TYPE;\n  workspaceId: string; userId: string; occurredAt: string;\n  unreadCount: number;\n  notifications: NotificationRealtimeEntry[];\n};\n```\nPublished per recipient by `.../services/notification-realtime-publisher.service.ts:27-53`, with `unreadCount` read back from `NotificationService.countUnread` (never a parallel counter).\n\nACL — `.../realtime-gateway/services/realtime-topic-authorization.service.ts:129-133`:\n```ts\nif (topicContext.kind === 'inbox' && isDefined(topicContext.userId)) {\n  if (topicContext.userId !== socketContext.userId) {\n    throw new Error('Inbox topics are scoped to the owning user');\n  }\n}\n```\nParser — `.../realtime-gateway/utils/parse-realtime-topic.util.ts:26-27` maps `inbox` → `{ kind: 'inbox', workspaceId, userId: rest[0] }`.\n\n### 4e. Exact front `buildInboxTopic` to add\nCreate `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/inbox/utils/buildInboxTopic.ts`, mirroring `buildChatChannelTopic`:\n```ts\n// Inbox realtime topics follow the gateway grammar `workspace:<id>:inbox:<userId>`\n// (server parse-realtime-topic.util.ts). The builder mirrors the server\n// `inbox-topic.util.ts` so subscribe and publish name the topic identically.\nexport const buildInboxTopic = ({\n  workspaceId,\n  userId,\n}: {\n  workspaceId: string;\n  userId: string;\n}): string => `workspace:${workspaceId}:inbox:${userId}`;\n```\n\nSubscribe call (note: `userId` is the **core User id**, not the workspaceMember id — the ACL compares against `payload.userId`). Use `currentUserState` (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/auth/states/currentUserState.ts:20`, `CurrentUser.id`) together with `currentWorkspaceState.id`:\n```ts\nconst currentWorkspace = useAtomStateValue(currentWorkspaceState);\nconst currentUser = useAtomStateValue(currentUserState);\nconst topic =\n  isDefined(currentWorkspace?.id) && isDefined(currentUser?.id)\n    ? buildInboxTopic({ workspaceId: currentWorkspace.id, userId: currentUser.id })\n    : '';\n\nuseRealtimeTopic<NotificationInboxRealtimeEvent>({\n  topic,\n  enabled: topic.length > 0,\n  onEvent: (event) => { /* fold event.notifications + event.unreadCount */ },\n});\n```\nYou will also need a client-side mirror of `NotificationInboxRealtimeEvent` (same reason as `ChatRealtimeEvent.ts:4-6`: domain events are not in codegen).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Lingui / Linaria conventions + aliases\n\n### 5a. Linaria `styled`\n`ChatPage.tsx:1,18-41`:\n```tsx\nimport { styled } from '@linaria/react';\nimport { themeCssVariables } from 'twenty-ui/theme-constants';\n\nconst StyledChatPage = styled.div`\n  display: flex;\n  flex: 1;\n  height: 100%;\n  min-height: 0;\n  width: 100%;\n`;\n```\nConditional props pattern — `ChatSidebar.tsx:47-72`:\n```tsx\nconst StyledChannelButton = styled.button<{ isSelected: boolean }>`\n  background: ${({ isSelected }) =>\n    isSelected ? themeCssVariables.background.transparent.medium : 'transparent'};\n  ...\n`;\n```\nAlways style via `themeCssVariables` (no raw hex).\n\n### 5b. Lingui\nIn components use the `t` macro from `useLingui`:\n`ChatPage.tsx:2,44,113` and `ChatSidebar.tsx:2,117,132,134`:\n```tsx\nimport { useLingui } from '@lingui/react/macro';\nconst { t } = useLingui();\n...\n<StyledEmptyState>{t`No channels yet`}</StyledEmptyState>\n```\nIn non-component `.ts` modules use the `msg` macro from `@lingui/core/macro`, e.g.\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/onboarding/constants/WelcomeTitleMessage.ts`:\n```ts\nimport { msg } from '@lingui/core/macro';\nexport const WELCOME_TITLE_MESSAGE = msg`Welcome to your workspace`;\n```\n(and arrays of `msg\\`…\\`` in `.../onboarding/constants/OnboardingInstallableApps.ts`).\n\nMessage-ID/catalog locations — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/lingui.config.ts`:\n```ts\ncatalogs: [{ path: '<rootDir>/src/locales/{locale}', include: ['src'] }],\ncatalogsMergePath: '<rootDir>/src/locales/generated/{locale}',\ncompileNamespace: 'ts',\nformat: formatter({ lineNumbers: false, printLinguiId: true }),\n```\nSo: source catalogs `packages/twenty-front/src/locales/*.po`, compiled TS in `packages/twenty-front/src/locales/generated/*.ts`. Regeneration via `lingui extract`/`compile`. Per `AGENTS.md` (\"Do not commit translation catalogs unless translations are the task\"), leave the `.po`/generated churn out of the commit.\n\n### 5c. Alias conventions\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/tsconfig.json:23-26`\n```json\n\"paths\": {\n  \"@/*\": [\"./src/modules/*\"],\n  \"~/*\": [\"./src/*\"]\n}\n```\nMirrored in `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/vite.config.ts:274-289` (comment explains wyw-in-js/Linaria requires the mirror).\n\nTherefore `~/modules/realtime/...` and `@/realtime/...` are **the same file**. Convention in practice:\n- Own feature module: `@/chat/...`, states via `@/ui/utilities/state/jotai/hooks/...`.\n- Cross-cutting modules that sit outside the feature: imported with the `~/` root form — `ChatPage.tsx:14` uses `~/modules/realtime/components/RealtimeReconnectBanner`; `ChatChannelConversation.tsx:21-23` uses `~/modules/realtime/...`; `ChatRealtimeEvent.ts` comment. Pages themselves are imported via `~/pages/...` (routing).\n- `import { isDefined } from 'twenty-shared/utils'` for guards; icons from `twenty-ui/icon`; theme from `twenty-ui/theme-constants`.\n\nFor Inbox, `@/inbox/...` for the feature module and `~/modules/realtime/...` for the hook is the matching choice.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Existing notification-related front code to reuse (and the gap)\n\n### 6a. Front primitives that exist\n- **Bell icon**: `IconBell` is exported from `twenty-ui/icon` (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-ui/src/icon/index.ts:89`) and is the canonical notification icon in the dictionary:\n  `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-ui/src/icon/constants/TwentyIconDictionary.ts:538-545`\n  ```\n  key: 'notification', label: 'Notification', iconName: 'IconBell',\n  keywords: ['notification', 'notice', 'notification settings', 'alert'],\n  useWhen: 'Representing notifications or notification settings.',\n  ```\n  (`icon-dictionary.md:115`). There is **no `inbox` dictionary key**; `IconNotification`/`IconBell` are available in `AllIcons.ts`.\n- **Unread/badge counter**: `NotificationCounter` in `twenty-ui/data-display` (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-ui/src/data-display/NotificationCounter/NotificationCounter.tsx`), exported from `.../data-display/index.ts:36`. Currently used only by `.../record-drag/components/RecordDragMultiDragCounterChip.tsx:4,28` — **not** in any nav/shell.\n- **Chat's unread badge** is local (`ChatSidebar.tsx:86-95` `StyledUnreadBadge`), not the shared component.\n\n### 6b. What does NOT exist in the front\n- No `modules/notification` or `modules/inbox` directory (glob found none).\n- No `pages/**/*Inbox*`.\n- No notification preferences settings UI (the only \"Notifications\" strings are storybook/webhook copy, e.g. `.../settings/components/SettingsOptions/__stories__/SettingsOptionCardContentToggle.stories.tsx:48-49`).\n- No bell in the app shell / navigation drawer. `IconBell` appears only in stories and a mock command-menu item.\n- No notification GraphQL types in `src/generated-metadata/graphql.ts` (grep found none).\n- `NotificationCounter` and `IconBell` are the two real reusables.\n\n### 6c. Server backend that exists (P8.1) — but no GraphQL resolver\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/notification/`:\n- `notification.entity.ts` — core schema `notification` (`userId`, `type`, `payload`, `readAt`, `archivedAt`).\n- `services/notification.service.ts` — `findForUser` (`:176-193`), `countUnread` (`:195-205`), `markAsRead` (`:207-231`), `archiveNotification` (`:233-246`), `getPreferences`/`updatePreferences` (`:141-174`), `requestNotifications`/`dispatchNotifications`.\n- `utils/inbox-topic.util.ts`, `utils/notification-realtime-event.util.ts`, `services/notification-realtime-publisher.service.ts`.\n- `constants/notification-type.constant.ts` — `MENTION`, `CHAT_MESSAGE`, `ASSIGNED`, `WATCHED_RECORD_CHANGED`, `BUDGET_ALERT`, `INVOICE_OVERDUE`, `PAYMENT_RECEIVED`, `SYSTEM`.\n- `constants/notification-channel.constant.ts`, `notification-policy.constant.ts` (quiet hours/digest), `types/notification-preferences.type.ts`.\n\n**Critical gap**: a filesystem search under `packages/twenty-server/src` finds **no resolver/query file** for notifications (`find … *notification*resolver*` → empty), and `@Query`/`@Mutation` grep in the notification module → none. The phase report confirms this is deferred