      "errorMessage": "<task id=\"ses_f499ead2cffeG0w0yfJ87X3yLQ\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI have everything needed. Here is the complete research report.\n\n---\n\n# GraphQL resolver pattern for a core-schema entity (`notification`)\n\n## 1. Canonical pattern for a core-schema, user/workspace-scoped entity\n\nThe closest 1:1 analog is **`document-share`** (core `@Entity({ schema: 'core' })`, workspace + user scoped, `@CoreResolver`). DPA is the analog for returning a **core entity directly**.\n\n### File layout (`document-share`)\n```\npackages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/document-share/\n├── document-share.entity.ts\n├── document-share.service.ts\n├── document-share.resolver.ts          # @CoreResolver class, Query/Mutation methods\n├── document-share.module.ts            # registers resolver in providers[]\n├── document-share-exception.filter.ts\n├── document-share.exception.ts\n└── dtos/\n    ├── create-document-share.input.ts  # @InputType()\n    ├── document-share.dto.ts           # @ObjectType('DocumentShare')\n    └── guest-document-share.dto.ts\n```\nThere is no separate `*.query.ts`/`*.mutation.ts` file in this codebase; a single `*.resolver.ts` holds `@Query`/`@Mutation` methods (as in `dpa.resolver.ts:34-58`, `client-config.resolver.ts:25-49`).\n\n### Resolver decorators + user/workspace acquisition\n`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/document-share/document-share.resolver.ts:1-40`:\n```ts\nimport { UseFilters, UseGuards, UsePipes } from '@nestjs/common';\nimport { Args, Mutation, Query } from '@nestjs/graphql';\n\nimport { CoreResolver } from 'src/engine/api/graphql/graphql-config/decorators/core-resolver.decorator';\nimport { ResolverValidationPipe } from 'src/engine/core-modules/graphql/pipes/resolver-validation.pipe';\nimport { PreventNestToAutoLogGraphqlErrorsFilter } from 'src/engine/core-modules/graphql/filters/prevent-nest-to-auto-log-graphql-errors.filter';\nimport { WorkspaceEntity } from 'src/engine/core-modules/workspace/workspace.entity';\nimport { AuthWorkspace } from 'src/engine/decorators/auth/auth-workspace.decorator';\nimport { UserAuthGuard } from 'src/engine/guards/user-auth.guard';\nimport { WorkspaceAuthGuard } from 'src/engine/guards/workspace-auth.guard';\n\n// Without @CoreResolver the class never registers on the GraphQL schema and\n// every document-share endpoint silently 404s at the schema level.\n@CoreResolver()\n@UsePipes(ResolverValidationPipe)\n@UseFilters(DocumentShareExceptionFilter, PreventNestToAutoLogGraphqlErrorsFilter)\nexport class DocumentShareResolver {\n  constructor(private readonly documentShareService: DocumentShareService) {}\n\n  @Query(() => [DocumentShareDTO])\n  @UseGuards(WorkspaceAuthGuard, UserAuthGuard)\n  async findManyDocumentShares(\n    @AuthWorkspace() currentWorkspace: WorkspaceEntity,\n  ): Promise<DocumentShareDTO[]> { ... }\n\n  @Mutation(() => DocumentShareDTO)\n  @UseGuards(WorkspaceAuthGuard, UserAuthGuard)\n  async createDocumentShare(\n    @Args('createDocumentShareInput') createDocumentShareInput: CreateDocumentShareInput,\n    @AuthWorkspace() currentWorkspace: WorkspaceEntity,\n  ): Promise<DocumentShareDTO> { ... }\n```\n\nCurrent **user + workspace** together, exactly matching `NotificationService.findForUser({workspaceId, userId})` — `client-config.resolver.ts:16-35` and `timeline-messaging.resolver.ts:89-104`:\n```ts\n@UseGuards(WorkspaceAuthGuard, UserAuthGuard)\n@UsePipes(ResolverValidationPipe)\n@UseFilters(PreventNestToAutoLogGraphqlErrorsFilter)\n@CoreResolver()\nexport class ClientConfigResolver {\n  @Query(() => Boolean)\n  @UseGuards(NoPermissionGuard)\n  async isMaintenanceModeBannerDismissed(\n    @AuthUser() user: AuthContextUser,\n    @AuthWorkspace() workspace: WorkspaceEntity,\n  ): Promise<boolean> {\n    return this.maintenanceModeService.isMaintenanceModeBannerDismissed(user.id, workspace.id);\n  }\n```\n- `@AuthWorkspace()` → `request.workspace` (`src/engine/decorators/auth/auth-workspace.decorator.ts:13-28`); use `.id`.\n- `@AuthUser()` → `request.user` (`src/engine/decorators/auth/auth-user.decorator.ts:13-26`); use `.id`. Type is `AuthContextUser` from `src/engine/core-modules/auth/types/auth-context.type`.\n- `@AuthUserWorkspaceId()` (`src/engine/decorators/auth/auth-user-workspace-id.decorator.ts`) is available when you need the user-workspace join id instead.\n\n### Pagination / filter args\nTwo idioms, both in `timeline-messaging.resolver.ts:25-78`:\n```ts\n@ArgsType()\nclass GetTimelineThreadsFromObjectRecordArgs {\n  @Field(() => String) objectNameSingular: string;\n  @Field(() => UUIDScalarType) recordId: string;\n  @Field(() => Int) page: number;\n  @Field(() => Int) @Max(TIMELINE_THREADS_MAX_PAGE_SIZE) pageSize: number;\n}\n// used as: async get...(…, @Args() { objectNameSingular, recordId, page, pageSize }: Get...Args)\n```\nOr loose limit/offset with defaults (`admin-panel.resolver.ts:438-440`):\n```ts\n@Args('limit', { type: () => Int, nullable: true, defaultValue: 50 }) limit: number,\n@Args('offset', { type: () => Int, nullable: true, defaultValue: 0 }) offset: number,\n```\nA filter input object example: `application-connections.resolver.ts:29` — `@Args('filter', { nullable: true }) filter?: ListAppConnectionsInput`. Aggregate-with-total DTOs use `@CoreResolver(() => TimelineThreadsWithTotalDTO)` (`timeline-messaging.resolver.ts:81`) or `@CoreResolver(() => DpaAgreementEntity)` (`dpa.resolver.ts:22`).\n\n### DTO pattern (important for `NotificationEntity`)\n`document-share/dto/document-share.dto.ts:1-26`:\n```ts\nimport { Field, ObjectType } from '@nestjs/graphql';\nimport { UUIDScalarType, DateScalarType } from 'src/engine/api/graphql/workspace-schema-builder/graphql-types/scalars';\n\n@ObjectType('DocumentShare')\nexport class DocumentShareDTO {\n  @Field(() => UUIDScalarType) id: string;\n  @Field({ nullable: false }) shareToken: string;\n  // Explicit scalar type required: without it NestJS GraphQL fails schema\n  // generation with UndefinedTypeError for this nullable Date output.\n  @Field(() => DateScalarType, { nullable: true }) expiresAt: Date | null;\n  @Field() createdAt: Date;\n}\n```\nInput DTO: `@InputType()` + `@Field()` (`create-document-share.input.ts:1-32`).\n\n**Critical caveat for `NotificationEntity`:** it is decorated `@ObjectType('Notification')` (`notification.entity.ts:18`) but **none of its columns have `@Field()` decorators** — the inherited `workspaceId`/`workspace` from `WorkspaceRelatedEntity` (`workspace-manager/types/workspace-related-entity.ts:1-12`) don't either. Returning the entity directly from a resolver would produce an empty, invalid GraphQL object type. Two safe options:\n- Follow DPA: add `@Field(...)` to entity columns (DPA does this, `dpa/entities/dpa-agreement.entity.ts:30-84`), **or**\n- Follow document-share: add a `NotificationDTO` (`@ObjectType('Notification')` would collide with the entity's registered name, so use a distinct name or remove the entity's `@ObjectType`).\n- `payload: Record<string, unknown> | null` needs the `JSON` scalar; `GraphQLJSON` is globally registered in `graphql-config.service.ts:88` (`resolvers: { JSON: GraphQLJSON }`). `readAt`/`archivedAt`/`createdAt`/`updatedAt` need `DateScalarType` (nullable ones must be explicit, per the comment above).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Runtime schema wiring\n\nRegistration is **not automatic from `@ObjectType` alone** — it requires `@CoreResolver` + being a provider reachable from `CoreEngineModule`.\n\n`graphql-config.service.ts:83-94` (the core `/graphql` schema):\n```ts\nconst config: YogaDriverConfig = {\n  autoSchemaFile: true,\n  include: [CoreEngineModule],\n  resolverSchemaScope: 'core',\n  buildSchemaOptions: {},\n  resolvers: { JSON: GraphQLJSON },\n  ...\n  path: `/${ApiPath.GraphQL}`,\n```\nThe filtering happens inside `@nestjs/graphql`'s explorer (`node_modules/@nestjs/graphql/dist/services/resolvers-explorer.service.js:58-62` and `174-179`):\n```js\nconst resolverSchemaScope = this.gqlOptions.resolverSchemaScope;\nif (resolverSchemaScope && wrapper.metatype) {\n  // Default to 'metadata' for unscoped resolvers (e.g. nestjs-query auto-generated CRUD)\n  const resolverScope = Reflect.getMetadata(RESOLVER_SCHEMA_SCOPE_KEY, wrapper.metatype) || 'metadata';\n  if (resolverScope !== resolverSchemaScope) { return undefined; }\n}\n```\n`@CoreResolver()` is exactly `Resolver()` + `SetMetadata(RESOLVER_SCHEMA_SCOPE_KEY, 'core')`:\n```ts\n// packages/twenty-server/src/engine/api/graphql/graphql-config/decorators/core-resolver.decorator.ts:7-11\nexport const CoreResolver = (typeFunc?: () => unknown) =>\n  applyDecorators(\n    typeFunc ? Resolver(typeFunc) : Resolver(),\n    SetMetadata(RESOLVER_SCHEMA_SCOPE_KEY, 'core' as ResolverSchemaScope),\n  );\n```\nSo the rule: **add `@CoreResolver()`, then register the class in a module's `providers[]` that is transitively imported by `CoreEngineModule`.**\n\n`NotificationModule` is already imported by CoreEngineModule:\n- `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/core-engine.module.ts:57` — `import { NotificationModule } from 'src/engine/core-modules/notification/notification.module';`\n- `core-engine.module.ts:149` — `NotificationModule,` in `imports`.\n\n**Current `notification.module.ts` (`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/notification/notification.module.ts:1-24`):**\n```ts\nimport { Module } from '@nestjs/common';\nimport { TypeOrmModule } from '@nestjs/typeorm';\n\nimport { KeyValuePairModule } from 'src/engine/core-modules/key-value-pair/key-value-pair.module';\nimport { NotificationRequestedListener } from 'src/engine/core-modules/notification/listeners/notification-requested.listener';\nimport { NotificationEntity } from 'src/engine/core-modules/notification/notification.entity';\nimport { NotificationRealtimePublisherService } from 'src/engine/core-modules/notification/services/notification-realtime-publisher.service';\nimport { NotificationService } from 'src/engine/core-modules/notification/services/notification.service';\nimport { RealtimeGatewayModule } from 'src/engine/core-modules/realtime-gateway/realtime-gateway.module';\n\n@Module({\n  imports: [\n    KeyValuePairModule,\n    TypeOrmModule.forFeature([NotificationEntity]),\n    RealtimeGatewayModule,\n  ],\n  exports: [NotificationService],\n  providers: [\n    NotificationService,\n    NotificationRequestedListener,\n    NotificationRealtimePublisherService,\n  ],\n})\nexport class NotificationModule {}\n```\nNo resolver provider exists yet. The minimal change is adding an `import { NotificationResolver } ...` and listing it in `providers` (compare `document-share.module.ts:9-13`, which also adds nothing to `imports` beyond what's needed). No central resolver list needs editing.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Guard requirements / exact import paths\n\nA core resolver does **not** strictly require a guard to compile, but every user/workspace-scoped core resolver applies the same pair. Exact paths:\n\n```ts\nimport { CoreResolver } from 'src/engine/api/graphql/graphql-config/decorators/core-resolver.decorator';\nimport { AuthUser } from 'src/engine/decorators/auth/auth-user.decorator';\nimport { AuthWorkspace } from 'src/engine/decorators/auth/auth-workspace.decorator';\nimport { WorkspaceAuthGuard } from 'src/engine/guards/workspace-auth.guard';\nimport { UserAuthGuard } from 'src/engine/guards/user-auth.guard';\nimport { NoPermissionGuard } from 'src/engine/guards/no-permission.guard';\nimport { CustomPermissionGuard } from 'src/engine/guards/custom-permission.guard';\nimport { SettingsPermissionGuard } from 'src/engine/guards/settings-permission.guard';\nimport { PublicEndpointGuard } from 'src/engine/guards/public-endpoint.guard';\n```\n\n- `@CoreResolver()` is mandatory for `/graphql` registration (see §2). There is no `@UseGuards` requirement imposed by the schema scope.\n- `WorkspaceAuthGuard` (`src/engine/guards/workspace-auth.guard.ts:12-29`) asserts `request.workspace` exists.\n- `UserAuthGuard` (`src/engine/guards/user-auth.guard.ts:7-18`) asserts `request.user !== undefined` — required because your service is keyed by `userId`.\n- Apply at class level: `@UseGuards(WorkspaceAuthGuard, UserAuthGuard)` (document-share resolver, client-config resolver). Permission guards (`SettingsPermissionGuard(PermissionFlagType.X)`, `CustomPermissionGuard`) are added per-method for privileged actions (`timeline-messaging.resolver.ts:80,202`).\n- `@UsePipes(ResolverValidationPipe)` (`src/engine/core-modules/graphql/pipes/resolver-validation.pipe`) enables `class-validator` on args; `@UseFilters(PreventNestToAutoLogGraphqlErrorsFilter)` (`src/engine/core-modules/graphql/filters/prevent-nest-to-auto-log-graphql-errors.filter`) is the standard filter. DPA additionally uses `AuthGraphqlApiExceptionFilter` and `PermissionsGraphqlApiExceptionFilter` (`dpa.resolver.ts:7,20,23`).\n\nFor a `notification` resolver returning only the caller's own rows, `@UseGuards(WorkspaceAuthGuard, UserAuthGuard)` + `@UsePipes(ResolverValidationPipe)` + `@UseFilters(PreventNestToAutoLogGraphqlErrorsFilter)` + `@CoreResolver()` matches the house pattern.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Front-end GraphQL types generation\n\n### Core (non-metadata) codegen config\n`packages/twenty-front/codegen.cjs:3-34` — schema is the **live core `/graphql` endpoint**, output `src/generated/graphql.ts`:\n```js\nmodule.exports = {\n  schema: (process.env.REACT_APP_SERVER_BASE_URL ?? 'http://localhost:3000') + '/graphql',\n  documents: [\n    './src/modules/workflow/**/graphql/**/*.{ts,tsx}',\n    './src/modules/object-core/**/graphql/**/*.{ts,tsx}',\n    './src/modules/activities/emails/graphql/queries/**/*.{ts,tsx}',\n    './src/modules/activities/calendar/graphql/queries/**/*.{ts,tsx}',\n    './src/modules/search/graphql/**/*.{ts,tsx}',\n    './src/modules/command-menu/graphql/**/*.{ts,tsx}',\n    '!./src/**/*.test.{ts,tsx}', ...\n  ],\n  overwrite: true,\n  generates: {\n    './src/generated/graphql.ts': {\n      plugins: ['typescript', 'typescript-operations', 'typed-document-node'],\n      config: { skipTypename: false, defaultScalarType: 'any',\n        scalars: { DateTime: 'string' }, namingConvention: { enumValues: 'keep' } },\n    },\n  },\n};\n```\nConfig selection — `packages/twenty-front/project.json:252-270`:\n```jsonc\n\"graphql:generate\": {\n  \"executor\": \"nx:run-commands\",\n  \"defaultConfiguration\": \"data\",\n  \"options\": { \"cwd\": \"{projectRoot}\", \"command\": \"dotenv graphql-codegen -- --config={args.config}\" },\n  \"configurations\": {\n    \"data\":     { \"config\": \"codegen.cjs\" },          // -> src/generated/graphql.ts          (core /graphql)\n    \"metadata\": { \"config\": \"codegen-metadata.cjs\" }, // -> src/generated-metadata/graphql.ts (/metadata)\n    \"admin\":    { \"config\": \"codegen-admin.cjs\" }     // -> src/generated-admin/graphql.ts    (/admin-panel)\n  }\n}\n```\nRun: `npx nx run twenty-front:graphql:generate` (default = data/core) — requires the server running. The generated core file is **checked in** at `packages/twenty-front/src/generated/graphql.ts` (~95 KB).\n\n### Example core query document → generated output\nOperation document `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/activities/calendar/graphql/queries/getTimelineCalendarEventsFromObjectRecord.ts:1-21`:\n```ts\nimport { gql } from '@apollo/client';\nexport const getTimelineCalendarEventsFromObjectRecord = gql`\n  query GetTimelineCalendarEventsFromObjectRecord(\n    $objectNameSingular: String! $recordId: UUID! $page: Int! $pageSize: Int!\n  ) {\n    getTimelineCalendarEventsFromObjectRecord(...) { ...TimelineCalendarEventsWithTotalFragment }\n  }\n  ${timelineCalendarEventWithTotalFragment}\n`;\n```\nGenerated in `src/generated/graphql.ts`:\n- `graphql.ts:877` — `GetTimelineCalendarEventsFromObjectRecordQueryVariables`\n- `graphql.ts:885` — `GetTimelineCalendarEventsFromObjectRecordQuery` (typed result)\n- `graphql.ts:1097` — `GetTimelineCalendarEventsFromObjectRecordDocument` (`TypedDocumentNode`)\n\n### Two accepted modes for a **new** core module\n1. **Codegen-tracked:** create `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/<module>/graphql/queries|mutations/*.ts` with a `gql` document, add a glob for that directory to `codegen.cjs` `documents[]`, then run `npx nx run twenty-front:graphql:generate`. (DPA had to be *excluded* from metadata codegen for exactly this reason — `codegen-metadata.cjs:20-22`.)\n2. **Hand-written (used for recently added core endpoints not yet in a codegen glob):** DPA — `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/legal/graphql/queries/getDpaAgreements.ts:1-20` defines the `gql` document via `graphql-tag`, and `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/legal/types/Dpa.ts:1-39` hand-types the result to mirror the server DTO; the glob is deliberately excluded from `codegen-metadata.cjs`. Document-share does the same: `modules/document-share/graphql/queries/getGuestDocumentShare.ts:1-15` plus a local `GuestDocumentShare` type in `hooks/useGuestDocumentShare.ts:7-35`. Comments in these files explicitly say \"Hand-written until the GraphQL schema codegen regenerates\".\n\n**Recommendation for `notification`:** add `./src/modules/notification/graphql/**/*.{ts,tsx}` (or similar) to `codegen.cjs` and generate into `src/generated/graphql.ts`; otherwise follow the DPA/document-share hand-written pattern. Either works; the DPA path avoids needing a running server in the same change.\n\n---\n\n## Summary of the exact pattern to replicate\n\n| Concern | Answer / analog |\n|---|---|\n| Resolver filename | `notification/notification.resolver.ts`, one class, `@Query`/`@Mutation` methods |\n| DTOs | `notification/dtos/*.dto.ts` (`@ObjectType`) and `*.input.ts` (`@InputType`); entity lacks `@Field`s, so DTO or add `@Field`s |\n| Required class decorator | `@CoreResolver()` from `src/engine/api/graphql/graphql-config/decorators/core-resolver.decorator` |\n| Guards | `@UseGuards(WorkspaceAuthGuard, UserAuthGuard)`; + `@UsePipes(ResolverValidationPipe)` + `@UseFilters(PreventNestToAutoLogGraphqlErrorsFilter)` |\n| Current user / workspace | `@AuthUser() user: AuthContextUser` → `user.id`; `@AuthWorkspace() workspace: WorkspaceEntity` → `workspace.id` |\n| Module registration | add resolver to `providers[]` in `notification.module.ts`; `NotificationModule` is already in `CoreEngineModule` imports (`core-engine.module.ts:149`), and core schema uses `include: [CoreEngineModule]`, `resolverSchemaScope: 'core'` (`graphql-config.service.ts:85-86`) |\n| No central list to edit | schema scope filtering is via `RESOLVER_SCHEMA_SCOPE` metadata in `@nestjs/graphql`'s resolver explorer |\n| Front-end | `codegen.cjs` (schema `/graphql`, output `src/generated/graphql.ts`) — add a document glob and run `npx nx run twenty-front:graphql:generate`; or hand-write document + local types like DPA/document-share |\n</task_result>\n</task>",
