/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/docs/plan/phases/phase-08-report.md:26`\n> \"Read/archive-side badge decrement is not wired: `markAsRead`/`archiveNotification` have no caller yet (P8.2 inbox resolver)…\"\n\nSo a front-only Inbox page cannot list/read notifications through GraphQL yet. You either add the P8.2 resolver (server) or scope the page to realtime-only data. P8.2 plan is in `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/PLAN.md:1239-1256`:\n```\n- [ ] Realtime push on `workspace:<id>:inbox:<userId>`; unread badge counts\n- [ ] Preference model per user (per-type channel: inbox/email/none)\n### P8.2 UX\n- [ ] Inbox app/page: filters (all/mentions/assigned/watching), grouped by …\n```\nAnd `phase-08-report.md:29` names your exact next step:\n> \"Next: P8.2 inbox app/page consuming `NotificationService.findForUser`/`countUnread` + subscribing the inbox topic with the P2.2 `useRealtimeTopic` primitive (build the matching front `buildInboxTopic`)\"\n\n---\n\n## Summary of the precedent chain for your implementation\n\n| Concern | Chat precedent | Inbox action |\n|---|---|---|\n| `AppPath` | `twenty-shared/src/types/AppPath.ts:24` | add `Inbox = '/inbox'`; rebuild twenty-shared |\n| Route | `createWorkspaceRouteObjects.tsx:44-48,136-143` | lazy import `~/pages/inbox/InboxPage` + route object |\n| Query param | `ChatPage.tsx:45,63,67-93` | same `useSearchParams` + select effect |\n| Deep link | `mapChatSearchRecordsToResultItems.ts:16-17` | `getAppPath(AppPath.Inbox, undefined, { notificationId })` |\n| Nav entry | none in front; app VIEW item `a2e-chat/.../channels.navigation-menu-item.ts` | no front registry; use Cmd+K provider precedent (native route can't be a `LINK` item) |\n| Data | `useFindManyRecords` / `useQuery`+`useApolloCoreClient` | needs a new notifications GraphQL resolver (missing) |\n| Realtime | `buildChatChannelTopic.ts` + `useChatChannelLive.ts:90-134` | `buildInboxTopic.ts` (mirror server's) + `useRealtimeTopic<NotificationInboxRealtimeEvent>` with `currentWorkspaceState.id` + `currentUserState.id` |\n| Event type | `ChatRealtimeEvent.ts` client mirror | mirror `notification.inbox.updated` payload client-side |\n| Styling/i18n | Linaria `styled` + `t`/`msg` | same; catalogs in `src/locales`, don't commit |\n| Reuse | — | `IconBell` (`twenty-ui/icon`), `NotificationCounter` (`twenty-ui/data-display`) |\n| Aliases | `@/chat/...`, `~/modules/realtime/...` | `@/inbox/...`, `~/modules/realtime/...` |\n\nOne caveat to design around: the Inbox page is a **native hard-coded route**, consistent with the documented boundary that apps cannot add routes (`docs/plan/phases/phase-04-report.md:462-466`) and `docs/plan/04-twenty-native-law.md:104-106` (\"dedicated front page feature-flagged\").\n</task_result>\n</task>"
