        "prompt": "I'm working in the A2E Suite / Twenty monorepo at /Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite. I need to add a GraphQL resolver for a core-schema entity called `notification` (already exists as `NotificationEntity` in packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/notification/notification.entity.ts; service `NotificationService` has `findForUser`, `countUnread`, `markAsRead`, `archiveNotification`, `getPreferences`, `updatePreferences`).\n\nResearch and report (read-only, do NOT edit anything):\n\n1. The canonical pattern for exposing a **core-schema, user/workspace-scoped entity** through GraphQL in `packages/twenty-server`. Find a concrete analogous module (e.g. documentShare under core-modules, keyValuePair, or any core entity with a resolver) and show: file layout (`*.resolver.ts`, `*.query.ts`/`*.mutation.ts`, DTO classes, module registration), decorators used (`@Resolver`, `@Query`, `@Mutation`, `@UseGuards`, `@UseFilters`, `@AuthWorkspace`, `@AuthUser` etc.), how the current user + workspace are obtained in the resolver, and how pagination/filter args are declared.\n\n2. How core resolvers are wired into the GraphQL schema at runtime — is it automatic via NestJS decorators + `@ObjectType`? Is there a module list where `NotificationModule` (already imported in core-engine.module.ts) needs to register a resolver provider? Show the `notification.module.ts` current content.\n\n3. Whether core GraphQL resolvers require a `@CoreResolver`-like guard, workspace auth guard, or `@UseGuards(WorkspaceAuthGuard)`. Give exact import paths.\n\n4. How the front-end GraphQL types are generated: find `packages/twenty-front/src/generated/graphql.ts` (or similar), and the codegen config. Are core-module operations added manually as documents in `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/**/graphql/*.ts` and then codegen'd? Show an example for a core (non-metadata) query.\n\nReport file paths with line numbers and paste the key code snippets. Be thorough but focused on the res